# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY TRACKED, so that a later edit has to argue with a
# sentence before it can drop it:
#
#   results/*.jsonl  THE EVIDENCE. Every number in README.md is derived from
#                    these by scripts/check_readme_numbers.py, and CI fails if
#                    a figure stops matching. THREE runs of 1,860 rows --
#                    sweep.jsonl and sweep_openai.jsonl, one per model vendor,
#                    plus sweep_replicate.jsonl, a second run of the Claude
#                    configuration that is the only thing here measuring
#                    run-to-run variance. sweep.failures.jsonl is the
#                    retry log and is empty, which is the claim it makes.
#   cqa/             the world, the questions, the ten conditions, the grader
#                    and the governance detector
#   scripts/         the pre-flight gate, the runner, the reporter and the
#                    figure deriver
#   tests/           the suite, including the mutation-checked guards
#
# THE RESULTS ARE THE POINT AND THEY ARE SMALL. Under four megabytes of JSONL
# holds every generation: the answer, the per-field grade, the governance
# verdict, token usage, and a hash of the question set and of the condition
# that produced the row. Without them nothing in README.md can be
# checked by a reader, which is the whole reason they ship.
#
# Excluded below is only what a clone can rebuild.

envs
.venv
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
*.pyc
.DS_Store
